  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14058551/assets/5773f1515892d8eb2cb77c700eab48f7cf44b0f91e9e157960798574e23ca93d.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $g(x)$ is shown above. \nApproximate ${g}^{\u2032}(x)$ at the point $x=2$ using a backward difference approximation with step size $h=1.$",
  "worked_solution": "We use the backward difference approximation formula\n\n$$\n{g}^{\u2032}(x)\u2248\\frac{g(x)-g(x-h)}{h},\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=2.$ . Applying the above formula with $x=2$ and $h=1$ gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{\u2032}(2) & \u2248\\frac{g(2)-g(2-1)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(2)-g(1)}{1} \\\\  & =4-1 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
